      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Large Language Models (LLMs) and Prompt Engineering",
      "pageStart": 2,
      "pageEnd": 2,
      "target": "../sections/sec-005-large-language-models-llms-and-prompt-engineerin.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "LLMs are powerful deep learning models trained on large\ncorpora of text to perform a wide range of natural language\nprocessing tasks [27]–[29]. Prompt engineering is the task of\noptimizing the input prompt for an LLM to get the best results\nfrom it. Sahoo et al. [30] performed a systematic survey of\nprompt engineering techniques. For example, for new tasks\nwithout extensive prior training, few-shot training (providing\nthe model a few input-output examples) improves model per-\nformance on complex tasks, but requires additional tokens and\ncan lead to biases. Assigning the LLM a role or persona c",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Section II-D, LLMs and prompt engineering. Prompt engineering optimizes an LLM's input, and a survey by Sahoo and colleagues is cited. Few-shot examples help on complex new tasks but cost tokens and can bias results; assigning a role or persona can improve performance; splitting long instructional prompts into smaller subtasks helps; and detailed natural-language instructions outperform implicit task formulation.",
        "state": "draft",
