      "pageEnd": 3,
      "target": "../sections/sec-006-design-and-implementation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "In this section, we describe the design and implementation\nof our AI-assisted schema creation (Section III-A) and schema\nmatching (Section III-B) approaches.\nOur system communicates with LLMs via a configurable\nendpoint that follows the OpenAI API6. Users may select\nthe desired model via the application’s settings. Prompts are\nprogrammatically constructed and transmitted to the API, and\nthe resulting textual outputs are automatically parsed and\nprocessed by our application. Access to LLMs via these APIs\nrequires an authentication key tied to a user account and billing\nconfiguration. We do not",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Opening of Section III, design and implementation. The system talks to LLMs through a configurable endpoint that follows the OpenAI API; users choose the model in settings and must supply their own API key, since none is provided. Prompts are built programmatically and the outputs parsed automatically. All interactions and evaluations in the paper used gpt-4o-mini, chosen for its cost-efficiency and its proficiency with JSON Schema tasks.",
