      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "AI-assisted JSON Schema Creation",
      "pageStart": 3,
      "pageEnd": 3,
      "target": "../sections/sec-007-ai-assisted-json-schema-creation.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "MetaConfigurator’s modular and extensible architecture en-\nables the integration of a new AI assistance view. To enable\nschema creation and modifications via natural language, we\nintroduce a conversational, chat-like interface. Our hybrid\nmethod offers several advantages over pure LLM-based so-\nlutions:\n1) Prompt construction and context management: The\ntool handles all aspects of prompt engineering. For\nschema creation, it dynamically constructs a structured\nprompt that sets the LLM’s role (e.g., ”You are a JSON\nSchema expert”), includes the user’s natural language\ndescription, and specifies",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Section III-A, AI-assisted JSON Schema creation. A new chat-like AI assistance view lets users create and modify schemas in natural language. The hybrid method's five claimed advantages: the tool builds the prompt (setting a role such as \"You are a JSON Schema expert\", adding the description and the expected output format, and for modifications only the selected part of the schema); the result is validated at once and shown in the schema editor; sending only the selected sub-schema avoids errors on large schemas; formatting artefacts such as code fences are removed automatically; and when the output is incomplete or wrong the user sees the raw response and can fix it before accepting or discarding the change. Figure 1 shows a description turned into a schema and Figure 2 a modification; the same interface can query schemas and create, edit and query instances.",
        "state": "draft",
