      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Conclusion",
      "pageStart": 4,
      "pageEnd": 5,
      "target": "../sections/sec-010-conclusion.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "We presented a hybrid approach for schema creation,\nediting, and instance transformation using large language\nmodels, integrated into the open-source tool MetaConfigu-\nrator. Our method combines modular prompt engineering,\ntargeted context scoping, human-in-the-loop refinement, and\npost-processing safeguards to enable intuitive and controlled\nschema modeling. To enable transforming also large document\ninstances to satisfy a target schema, mapping rules are gener-\nated by LLMs but then applied in a deterministic manner.\nAn example in the chemistry domain demonstrates the\napplicability of our ap",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Conclusion and acknowledgment. The authors summarise a hybrid approach to schema creation, editing and instance transformation in MetaConfigurator that combines modular prompt engineering, targeted context, human-in-the-loop refinement and post-processing safeguards, with LLM-generated mapping rules applied deterministically so that large documents can be transformed. They argue the chemistry example shows support for FAIR data practices and model-driven workflows, note that the tool also supports validation, code and documentation generation, mapping discovery and form generation, and plan model-to-model transformations such as XSD to JSON Schema. Esengül Ciftci and Kenichi Endo are thanked for inspiring the example, and ChatGPT-4 is acknowledged for editorial suggestions.",
